            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for a heel, then the Russian for a palm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: висок",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "висок (visók) — \"a temple (of the head)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "У него седые волосы на висках. U negó sedýye vólosy na viskákh. He has grey hair at the temples."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; genitive виска, plural виски (stress on the end). Not to be confused with виски — whisky."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "EtymDB lists висок (visók) without a source; it is usually linked to висеть 'to hang', after the hair that hangs at the temples, but the link is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
